Auto Resolution @PROJECT_VERSION@ corresponding source

Plugin source: https://github.com/QTR-Modding/AutoResolution/tree/@SOURCE_REVISION@
CommonLibSSE-NG: https://github.com/alandtse/CommonLibSSE-NG/tree/39f9d07a6ffabea8fb559eee87ab7d27cd463e8a
OpenVR: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/openvr/tree/60eb187801956ad277f1cae6680e3a410ee0873b
hde64: https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook/tree/v1.3.4/src/hde
vcpkg dependency recipes: https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/tree/ee12231b20c95013c6638d845d04c91559a1d1ff

To retrieve the exact plugin and submodule sources:
  git clone https://github.com/QTR-Modding/AutoResolution.git
  cd AutoResolution
  git checkout @SOURCE_REVISION@
  git submodule update --init --recursive

Install Visual Studio with the x64 C++ tools, C++23 support and Windows SDK,
CMake, Ninja, and vcpkg. Set VCPKG_ROOT to the vcpkg directory. In an x64
Visual Studio developer shell:
  cmake --preset release
  cmake --build build/release --parallel
  cmake --install build/release --component AutoResolution --prefix build/package

Configuration retrieves hde64 at MinHook v1.3.4. vcpkg retrieves dependencies
at the manifest's pinned baseline, either from source or its binary cache.
For dependency sources, use a fresh build directory with the environment
variable VCPKG_BINARY_SOURCES set to clear before configuration. The sources
are then under vcpkg's buildtrees and build/release/_deps/hde64-src. The recipes
above give their source URLs and checksums.
